{"vid":"gcW6ziRcWv4","source":"gcW6ziRcWv4.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":1.4,"txt":"Okay, Monica, you know what? Hi, you're"},{"t":3,"txt":"kind of losing it here. I mean, this is"},{"t":4.3,"txt":"really becoming like a weird obsession"},{"t":6.1,"txt":"thing. This is madness. It's madness, I"},{"t":8.5,"txt":"tell you. FOR THE LOVE OF GOD, MONICA,"},{"t":10.1,"txt":"DON'T DO IT."},{"t":11.2,"txt":">> Do you sound like a polite robot even"},{"t":13.4,"txt":"when you're absolutely furious? Let's"},{"t":16,"txt":"fix that awkwardness right now. Stick"},{"t":18.2,"txt":"around."},{"t":27.2,"txt":"bought. Still, it's just such reckless"},{"t":29.8,"txt":"spending."},{"t":30.6,"txt":">> I think when somebody steals your credit"},{"t":32.6,"txt":"card, they've kind of already thrown"},{"t":34.2,"txt":"caution to the wind."},{"t":39,"txt":">> Wow, what a geek. They spent $69.95 on a"},{"t":42.4,"txt":"Wonder Mop."},{"t":47.5,"txt":">> You bought still such reckless spending."},{"t":51,"txt":">> I think"},{"t":51.5,"txt":">> reckless."},{"t":53.4,"txt":"Reckless describes actions taken without"},{"t":55.5,"txt":"thinking about the bad consequences. It"},{"t":58,"txt":"means careless or dangerous. Use it when"},{"t":60.4,"txt":"someone is taking unnecessary risks."},{"t":63.6,"txt":"He was arrested for reckless driving on"},{"t":65.4,"txt":"the highway. It describes driving"},{"t":67.8,"txt":"dangerously without care for safety."},{"t":71.6,"txt":">> When somebody steals your credit card,"},{"t":73.6,"txt":"they've kind of already thrown caution"},{"t":75.3,"txt":"to the wind."},{"t":77.7,"txt":">> Thrown caution to the wind. To throw"},{"t":80.5,"txt":"caution to the wind is a beautiful C2"},{"t":82.8,"txt":"idiom. It means to stop worrying about"},{"t":85,"txt":"risks and do something bold or"},{"t":86.6,"txt":"impulsive. It's perfect for describing"},{"t":88.9,"txt":"moments of pure freedom."},{"t":91.4,"txt":"She threw caution to the wind and moved"},{"t":93,"txt":"to Paris without a job. It means she"},{"t":95.5,"txt":"took a huge risk to follow her dream."},{"t":100.7,"txt":">> Wow, what a geek. They spent $69.95 on a"},{"t":104.1,"txt":"wonder mop."},{"t":106.6,"txt":">> Geek."},{"t":108.2,"txt":"Geek is a common slang term. Originally"},{"t":110.7,"txt":"an insult for social outcasts, it now"},{"t":112.7,"txt":"often affectionately describes someone"},{"t":114.5,"txt":"obsessed with a niche hobby, or in this"},{"t":116.9,"txt":"case, someone uncool because they bought"},{"t":118.6,"txt":"a mop."},{"t":120.3,"txt":"I'm a total history geek. I love"},{"t":122,"txt":"visiting museums. It expresses a strong"},{"t":125.1,"txt":"enthusiastic interest in a specific"},{"t":127,"txt":"subject."},{"t":134.1,"txt":">> Stalin, do I know that name? That sounds"},{"t":136,"txt":"familiar. Well, it does not ring a bell"},{"t":138,"txt":"with me."},{"t":140.5,"txt":">> Joe Stone,"},{"t":145.6,"txt":">> you know, that's pretty good."},{"t":151,"txt":">> That sounds familiar. Well, it does not"},{"t":153,"txt":"ring a bell with me."},{"t":156,"txt":">> Ring a bell. To ring a bell means that"},{"t":159.5,"txt":"something sounds familiar, but you can't"},{"t":161.5,"txt":"quite remember the details. It triggers"},{"t":163.9,"txt":"a distant memory. This is essential for"},{"t":166.2,"txt":"native level conversation."},{"t":168.9,"txt":"His face rings a bell, but I forget his"},{"t":170.8,"txt":"name. It means he looks familiar, but"},{"t":173.4,"txt":"the speaker can't place him."},{"t":177.8,"txt":">> You know, that's pretty good."},{"t":180.3,"txt":"You might"},{"t":181,"txt":">> pretty good. Pretty here doesn't mean"},{"t":184,"txt":"beautiful. It acts as a modifier meaning"},{"t":186.3,"txt":"moderately or quite. Pretty good is a"},{"t":189.4,"txt":"very natural, understated way to say"},{"t":191.4,"txt":"something is impressive."},{"t":194,"txt":"The movie was pretty good. Better than I"},{"t":195.8,"txt":"expected. It expresses that the movie"},{"t":198.5,"txt":"was enjoyable and decent,"},{"t":205.1,"txt":">> right?"},{"t":206.9,"txt":"But that may just be a pipe dream"},{"t":208.8,"txt":"because, you know, he's out of state."},{"t":213.1,"txt":"Uh my my vet uh knows someone at Miami."},{"t":215.9,"txt":"So So that's a possibility."},{"t":217.7,"txt":">> Yeah, but that's like two blocks away"},{"t":219.2,"txt":"from the beach. I mean, it's a total"},{"t":220.7,"txt":"party zoo."},{"t":224.6,"txt":"Right."},{"t":226.3,"txt":"But that may just be a pipe dream"},{"t":228.3,"txt":"because you know he's out of state."},{"t":231.4,"txt":">> Pipe dream. A pipe dream is a fantastic"},{"t":234.8,"txt":"hope or plan that is impossible to"},{"t":236.6,"txt":"achieve. It suggests an idea is just an"},{"t":239.3,"txt":"illusion. Use this to describe"},{"t":241.4,"txt":"unrealistic goals with a sophisticated"},{"t":243.4,"txt":"touch."},{"t":245,"txt":"His plan to become a billionaire"},{"t":246.5,"txt":"overnight is just a pipe dream. It"},{"t":249,"txt":"describes a goal that has zero chance of"},{"t":250.9,"txt":"happening."},{"t":253.4,"txt":"Out of state."},{"t":255.4,"txt":"Out of state refers to something or"},{"t":257.3,"txt":"someone from a different US state. In"},{"t":259.8,"txt":"America, tuition and regulations often"},{"t":262.2,"txt":"differ if you are instate versus out of"},{"t":264.4,"txt":"state."},{"t":266.1,"txt":"Out of state tuition is much more"},{"t":267.7,"txt":"expensive. It highlights the cost"},{"t":270.2,"txt":"difference based on residency."},{"t":284.2,"txt":"Okay, Monica, you know what? Hi, you're"},{"t":285.9,"txt":"kind of losing it here. I mean, this is"},{"t":287.3,"txt":"really becoming like a weird obsession"},{"t":289,"txt":"thing. This is madness. It's madness, I"},{"t":291.4,"txt":"tell you. FOR THE LOVE OF GOD, MONICA,"},{"t":297.8,"txt":">> OKAY, MONICA, you know what, huh? You're"},{"t":299.4,"txt":"kind of losing it here. I mean, this"},{"t":300.7,"txt":"losing it."},{"t":302.6,"txt":"Losing it means losing control of your"},{"t":304.9,"txt":"emotions or sanity. It can mean you are"},{"t":307.7,"txt":"becoming angry, crazy, or overly"},{"t":310.3,"txt":"emotional. It's very common in arguments"},{"t":313,"txt":"or high stress situations."},{"t":316.2,"txt":"He started losing it when he couldn't"},{"t":318,"txt":"find his keys."},{"t":320,"txt":"It shows he was becoming irrationally"},{"t":322.4,"txt":"angry or panicked."},{"t":325.7,"txt":">> But you know what, huh? You're kind of"},{"t":326.9,"txt":"losing it here. I mean, this is really"},{"t":328.3,"txt":"becoming like a weird obsession thing."},{"t":330.5,"txt":"Obsession."},{"t":332.8,"txt":"An obsession is a persistent dominating"},{"t":335.6,"txt":"thought or interest. Here it describes"},{"t":338.5,"txt":"Monica's unhealthy fixation on the woman"},{"t":341,"txt":"who stole her credit card."},{"t":343.9,"txt":"Her obsession with cleanliness makes her"},{"t":346.2,"txt":"house spotless."},{"t":348.2,"txt":"It describes an intense constant focus"},{"t":350.9,"txt":"on cleaning."},{"t":353.8,"txt":">> Madness. It's madness. I tell you, FOR"},{"t":355.6,"txt":"THE LOVE OF GOD, MONICA, DON'T DO IT."},{"t":357.9,"txt":"For the love of God."},{"t":360.6,"txt":"For the love of God is a dramatic phrase"},{"t":363.4,"txt":"used to express frustration, annoyance,"},{"t":366.3,"txt":"or urgency. It adds intense emotional"},{"t":369.4,"txt":"weight to a request. Use it when you are"},{"t":372.3,"txt":"desperate."},{"t":374.2,"txt":"For the love of God, please stop"},{"t":376.3,"txt":"singing. It expresses extreme annoyance"},{"t":379.8,"txt":"in a desperate plea to stop."},{"t":388.1,"txt":"I don't know who this is harder on. Me"},{"t":390.1,"txt":"or him?"},{"t":392.5,"txt":">> I'd say that chair is taking the brunt"},{"t":394.2,"txt":"of"},{"t":397.6,"txt":">> Marcel. Marcel."},{"t":403,"txt":">> I'd say that chair is taking the brunt"},{"t":404.8,"txt":"of taking the brunt. To 